    <h1>VPN for French Expats</h1>
    <p class="article-intro">Living abroad but need secure access from France? Whether it's for online banking, administrative tasks, or simply browsing safely, a VPN with a France-based server is essential.</p>

    <h2>Why Expats Need a French VPN</h2>
    <p>Living outside France creates real, frustrating situations:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Online banking</strong> — Some French banks detect foreign connections and block access or trigger complicated authentication flows.</li>
      <li><strong>Administrative portals</strong> — Government sites like impots.gouv.fr or ameli.fr can be slow or blocked depending on your country.</li>
      <li><strong>Security on local Wi-Fi</strong> — Public networks abroad (hotels, cafés, airports) are often poorly secured. A VPN encrypts all your traffic.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What VulcainVPN Offers Expats</h2>
    <p>VulcainVPN is an independent VPN service with a <strong>dedicated server in France</strong>. Unlike large providers that share servers among thousands of users, we deliberately limit our subscriber count to ensure consistent performance.</p>

    <div class="article-highlight">
      <h3>Key Points</h3>
      <p><span class="checkmark">➤</span> <strong>Dedicated France server</strong> — your traffic routes through France, not shared hubs in Amsterdam or Frankfurt</p>
      <p><span class="checkmark">➤</span> <strong>Multiple protocols</strong> — WireGuard for speed, Hysteria2 and Shadowsocks for difficult networks</p>
      <p><span class="checkmark">➤</span> <strong>No browsing logs</strong> — we don't store what you do online. <a href="<%= logging_path %>">See our logging policy</a></p>
      <p><span class="checkmark">➤</span> <strong>3 simultaneous devices</strong> — phone, laptop, tablet covered under one subscription</p>
    </div>

    <h2>Banking Apps and VPNs: What You Need to Know</h2>
    <p>Some French banks restrict VPN connections for security reasons. If your banking app blocks the connection, temporarily disable the VPN for that specific task. For everything else, keep the VPN on.</p>
    <p>This is a banking sector limitation, not a VPN issue — and not all banks behave the same way.</p>

    <h2>Available on Android and Windows</h2>
